# Margin Without the Sidebar

## Results
  {:label: sec-results}

A graph on $n$ vertices with no triangle has at most $n^2/4$ edges. The bound is
reached by a :aside:bip,complete bipartite graph:: with two equal parts. More text
follows here so that the paragraph has a few lines and a clear right edge.

:aside: {:label: bip}
A graph whose vertices are split into two parts, with an edge between every
pair of vertices in different parts.
::

A paragraph between the aside and the figure, long enough to wrap onto a second
line at any reading width.

